## Solana Infrastructure

### Light Protocol (ZK Compression)

-   **Docs:** https://www.zkcompression.com/
-   **Whitepaper:** https://www.zkcompression.com/introduction
-   **GitHub:** https://github.com/Lightprotocol/light-protocol
-   State compression using Merkle trees
-   200x cheaper account creation
-   **Potential use:** Commitment tree storage

Key features:

-   Compressed accounts (rent-free)
-   Merkle proofs for state verification
-   Interoperable with SPL tokens

### Helius (ZK Compression API)

-   **Docs:** https://www.helius.dev/docs/api-reference/zk-compression/overview
-   **Get Compressed Account:** https://www.helius.dev/docs/api-reference/zk-compression/getcompressedaccount
-   RPC methods for compressed state
-   **Use when:** Integrating with Light Protocol

Key endpoints:

-   `getCompressedAccount` - Fetch compressed account by address/hash
-   `getCompressedAccountProof` - Get Merkle proof
-   `getCompressedAccountsByOwner` - List accounts

### groth16-solana

-   **GitHub:** https://github.com/Lightprotocol/groth16-solana
-   Reference for BN254 syscall patterns
-   ~81K CU Groth16 verification

### Solana BN254 Syscalls

-   `solana-bn254` crate
-   Operations: addition, multiplication, pairing
-   All operations use big-endian bytes
-   Active on mainnet since Solana 1.18.x

